cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "evidencestale: measuring the stale fraction of an assurance case"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Measures how much of an assurance case rests on evidence whose subject has
  changed since the evidence was produced. A traceability tool checks that a
  link between a claim and its evidence exists; this checks whether the link is
  still true. Three methods are reported: a modification-revision comparison, a
  SHA-256 comparison over the dependency closure of each artifact, and a
  replayed change history in which each item's staleness is known by
  construction. A learned staleness-risk model over graph features is
  benchmarked against them on held-out artifacts and held-out time separately.
  Research-grade software; not flight-qualified, not certified and not approved
  for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - assurance case
  - safety case
  - goal structuring notation
  - traceability
  - evidence staleness
  - dependency closure
  - content hash
  - graph reachability
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/evidencestale"
